Decide how the summarizer should treat each child of one chunk-tree level.
Exactly one question is asked per child, in document order, and each
question names the child, its heading, and its size.

Answer each question with exactly one of these six options:

- expand: the child holds distinct dense content the task needs — it is
  summarized in full.
- summarize: the child's branch is homogeneous — one summary of the branch
  suffices, the summarizer decides the details.
- skip_boilerplate: boilerplate — navigation, headers, footers, legal or
  template filler with no task content.
- skip_appendix: appendix or reference material — cited, not read.
- skip_repeated: repeated material — the same content appears under another
  child that is expanded or summarized.
- skip_other: anything else never summarized.

The skip variants carry the reason, so no second question and no free text
is ever asked for. Be conservative: an ambiguous child is expanded or
summarized, never skipped — a skipped branch is invisible to the summary.
When the node budget for expansions is tight, prefer summarize over expand
for branches the task needs only in passing.
